§§ `Endnote [1], [2] and [5]: the instruments that amend Article 1, Article 2(1) and Schedule 1`

#ASSERT `the identifiers of` `the instruments that amend Article 1 (endnote [1])` EQUALS LIST "R&O.40/2019", "L.13/2019", "R&O.29/2021", "R&O.28/2023", "R&O.10/2024", "R&O.102/2026"
#ASSERT `the identifiers of` `the instruments that amend Article 2(1) (endnote [2])` EQUALS LIST "R&O.56/2025"
#ASSERT `the identifiers of` `the instruments that amend Schedule 1 (endnote [5])` EQUALS LIST "L.1/2017"
-- Eight amending instruments, nine texts (the first text is the Law as the remainder brought it into force, R&O.17/2018 Article 2).
#ASSERT count `the nine texts of the Law` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT count (mapMaybe (GIVEN row YIELD row's `brought by`) `the nine texts of the Law`) EQUALS 8
-- The only instrument that states a time of day is R&O.10/2024.
#ASSERT `a commencement takes effect partway through its day` (`R&O.10/2024`'s `comes into force`)
#ASSERT NOT `a commencement takes effect partway through its day` (`R&O.28/2023`'s `comes into force`)
#ASSERT NOT `a commencement takes effect partway through its day` (`R&O.102/2026`'s `comes into force`)
-- Which instruments are shown in the sources, and which date rests on the Table alone.
#ASSERT NOT `L.1/2017`'s `date in force shown by the sources`
#ASSERT `L.13/2019`'s `date in force shown by the sources`
#ASSERT count `the editorial changes of endnotes [3] and [4]` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT REFUSED `the first day on which a commencement is in force` (`a number of days after it is made` 7) NOTHING `fav`

